   "line": [
    "Bc4"
   ],
   "spoken": "A practical lesson: when you sense the opponent is steering into a line they know and you don't, you can sidestep the sharpest theory with a quiet move, accepting a slightly worse position in exchange for not being blown off the board. The principled tries here are the knight to f6 or clinging to the pawn with a bishop to c5.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 126,
   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/ppppbppp/2n5/8/2BpP3/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 2 5",
   "line": [
    "Be7"
   ],
   "spoken": "So opt for solid, even slightly passive chess — the bishop to e7, which also rules out an annoying knight lunge and lets development finish in peace.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 129.5,
   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/ppppbppp/2n5/8/2BpP3/2P2N2/PP3PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "c3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Here's a famous trap to know: grabbing the offered pawn is a blunder, because a queen leap to d5 threatens mate on f7 with no good defence — the only try drops a piece. So the pawn can't be taken, which leaves the standard menu of choices: ignore, accept, hand the pawn back on your own terms, or, failing all else, resign.",
   "kind": "tactic"
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 191,
   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/ppppbppp/2n5/8/2B1P3/2Pp1N2/PP3PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "d3"
   ],
   "spoken": "The choice here is to give the pawn back on favourable terms — a modest d3, denying the opponent a dominant pawn centre by forcing the capture rather than letting them build.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 205.5,
   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/ppppbppp/2n5/8/2B1P3/1QPp1N2/PP3PPP/RNB1K2R b KQkq - 1 6",
   "line": [
    "Qb3"
   ],
   "spoken": "The queen sortie to b3 is genuinely nasty, because the target pawn simply can't be held. The known antidote is a knight to a5, prising the queen away from the defence of the bishop and untangling by concrete means.",
   "kind": "tactic"
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 258,
   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/ppppbppp/8/n7/2B1P3/1QPp1N2/PP3PPP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 2 7",
   "line": [
    "Na5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
