   "line": [
    "Qd5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The tempting queen move to d5, keeping it lined up with the bishop, is actually a mistake — a pawn to c6 both attacks the queen and defends the knight in one move, and the queen is driven off with tempo. One move answering two threats.",
   "kind": "tactic"
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 292.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1knr/pp1pbBpp/2p5/n2Q4/4P3/2Pp1N2/PP3PPP/RNB1K2R w KQ - 0 9",
