   "line": [
    "Qe5"
   ],
   "spoken": "A queen to e5 induces a weakening pawn move in front of the king — and this is a lovely example of not needing a pawn storm. The open file has already been handed over, so pushing pawns would be counterproductive; the attack flows down the file as it is.",
