   "spoken": "A practical detour on suspicion of cheating: don't assume it after every clean loss — take the game to the engine. Accuracy only means much in longer games, and even a high score isn't proof, since strong cheaters often avoid the top move, picking the second or third to disguise it, and may toss in a deliberate mistake. Time spent per move and the opponent's game history tell you more; if a real case emerges, report it in good faith and let it be investigated.",
