   "spoken": "A subtle defensive idea worth naming: there's a common misconception that the queen leap wins a piece by fork — but forks must always be checked against a move that guards both threatened pieces at once. That's a defensive fork: instead of attacking two things, you defend two things in a single move, and it neutralises the whole idea.",
